Although the RNGs seem to spend most of their time torturing players, every
once in a great while, they'll exact delicious revenge on one of the
monsters instead.

By far my favorite happend in my latest game. I was on my way down to the
quest level. I had already cleared sokoban and the mines, netting boots of
speed, an amulet of reflection, and a blessed bag of holding. Normally, a
strong beginning like that is a recipe for some major RNG payback, usually
in the form of wands of death. Sure enough, on about dlvl 10:

The ogre lord zaps a short wand!  The death ray hits you!-- more --
But it reflects from your medallion!
The massive hammer hits!  Lightning strikes the ogre lord!
The ogre lord zaps a wand of death, which suddenly explodes!--more --
The ogre lord is killed!

Bwahahaha! Yeah, it was a wand of death alright, just not in the way he was
expecting! Now I've seen my share monsters wind up on the receiving end of
their own death ray plenty of times, but that's the first time I've ever
seen one get killed by the actual wand. Maybe next time he'll remember to
b/c/u ID his wands before zapping them indiscriminately.

The way things are going, I'm sure that I'll wind up getting killed by
choking on a fortune cookie or something, but you still have to savor those
moments when all the stars align just right and some dungeon nasty gets
exactly what's coming to him.



